# AetherSDR - CTR2 controller HID access for the active local user.
# 303A:1001 is Espressif's default for any ESP32-S3, so match the CTR2
# product strings too rather than opening every ESP32-S3 board. "Aether*" is
# controller firmware that speaks the CTR2 link and names itself; the app
# recognizes only a short printable name, so the glob grants a little more.
# The patterns must equal Ctr2HidPort::knownCtr2Devices();
# ctr2_proxy_model_test enforces it.
#
# The tty line is the CTR2-Max in download mode, for firmware installs from
# the CTR2 window: the ESP32-S3's built-in USB serial/JTAG port. Any ESP32-S3
# class board shows the same identity, in download mode and also under
# firmware that leaves USB to it, so the line opens that port on any such
# board to the seat's user. It cannot be narrowed to a CTR2.
#
# Installed by the build on Linux hidapi builds, and also installed on demand
# by the CTR2 window (via pkexec) for builds that did not ship it.
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="303a", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1001", ATTRS{product}=="ESP32S3_DEV|M5STACK_DIAL|STAMP-S3|AETHER_KNOB|Aether*", TAG+="uaccess"
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ATTRS{idVendor}=="2886", ATTRS{idProduct}=="0056", ATTRS{product}=="XIAO_ESP32S3", TAG+="uaccess"
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="303a", ATTRS{idProduct}=="1001", ATTRS{product}=="USB JTAG/serial debug unit", TAG+="uaccess"
